{"seq":32,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w25383"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish-mge card ppm-090, category 1; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Computer Science] What are the basic binary digits 0 and 1 also known as?\nA. Bytes B. Bits C. Bauds\nAnswer: B. The term “bit” is a contraction of “binary digit,” which is the most basic unit of data in computing and digital communications.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/mythology, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, earth-space/a","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish-mge/ppm-090.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"What is a single binary digit, 0 or 1, the most basic unit of information in computing, called?"},{"field":"de","new":"Wie heißt eine einzelne Binärziffer, 0 oder 1, die grundlegendste Informationseinheit in der Informatik?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish-mge","card":"ppm-090","category":1}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Computer Science] What are the basic binary digits 0 and 1 also known as?\nA. Bytes B. Bits C. Bauds\nAnswer: B. The term “bit” is a contraction of “binary digit,” which is the most basic unit of data in computing and digital communications."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f01244"}],"hash":"ee0e65569e22"},
